1
00:00:00,700 --> 00:00:03,113
A paper you know is relevant is missing

2
00:00:03,133 --> 00:00:04,259
from the results.

3
00:00:04,421 --> 00:00:06,630
Did the search misunderstand your words?

4
00:00:06,793 --> 00:00:08,899
Before adding a synonym or replacing the

5
00:00:08,919 --> 00:00:11,979
model, pause. The same screen could hide

6
00:00:11,999 --> 00:00:13,679
several different failures.

7
00:00:13,854 --> 00:00:15,612
What evidence would distinguish them?

8
00:00:18,044 --> 00:00:19,672
The chapter gives four alternative

9
00:00:19,692 --> 00:00:22,545
explanations: outside the collection,

10
00:00:22,695 --> 00:00:25,110
excluded by a filter, absent from the

11
00:00:25,130 --> 00:00:28,126
candidate pool, or retrieved but below the

12
00:00:28,146 --> 00:00:29,517
display boundary.

13
00:00:29,666 --> 00:00:32,417
Our diagrams show possible paths for the

14
00:00:32,437 --> 00:00:34,866
same hypothetical paper, not a traced

15
00:00:34,886 --> 00:00:35,651
search.

16
00:00:36,581 --> 00:00:38,018
Start with eligibility.

17
00:00:38,167 --> 00:00:40,660
Was the source covered, and had indexing

18
00:00:40,680 --> 00:00:43,276
caught up? Did a date condition, format

19
00:00:43,296 --> 00:00:46,575
facet or access filter exclude the record?

20
00:00:46,737 --> 00:00:49,217
A paper outside the searchable collection

21
00:00:49,237 --> 00:00:51,871
or eligible set was never in play.

22
00:00:52,033 --> 00:00:55,132
Vocabulary expansion cannot recover it

23
00:00:55,152 --> 00:00:57,425
through that unchanged boundary.

24
00:00:57,983 --> 00:01:00,710
Inspect coverage, limits and the record’s

25
00:01:00,730 --> 00:01:04,266
metadata. Some evidence is visible; some

26
00:01:04,286 --> 00:01:05,748
needs documentation.

27
00:01:05,923 --> 00:01:08,157
Record what remains unknown.

28
00:01:08,307 --> 00:01:11,212
An unavailable internal trace is not proof

29
00:01:11,232 --> 00:01:12,951
that the record was excluded.

30
00:01:13,867 --> 00:01:15,906
Now separate the candidate pool from the

31
00:01:15,926 --> 00:01:17,207
displayed results.

32
00:01:17,357 --> 00:01:19,875
An eligible paper can fail to enter the

33
00:01:19,895 --> 00:01:21,808
first stage shortlist.

34
00:01:21,957 --> 00:01:24,785
Investigate the query, indexed evidence,

35
00:01:24,805 --> 00:01:27,401
retrieval method and candidate cutoff.

36
00:01:27,550 --> 00:01:30,752
A later reranker cannot assess a paper it

37
00:01:30,772 --> 00:01:31,950
never received.

38
00:01:32,503 --> 00:01:35,115
A different paper may reach the pool and

39
00:01:35,135 --> 00:01:37,821
then fall below a later ranking or

40
00:01:37,841 --> 00:01:39,161
presentation limit.

41
00:01:39,336 --> 00:01:40,811
That is matched but hidden.

42
00:01:41,024 --> 00:01:43,646
Filter order and cutoff order can also

43
00:01:43,666 --> 00:01:45,475
change which records survive.

44
00:01:45,638 --> 00:01:48,453
A failed lookup alone does not identify

45
00:01:48,473 --> 00:01:49,973
the responsible boundary.

46
00:01:50,903 --> 00:01:52,504
Check the indexed unit too.

47
00:01:52,666 --> 00:01:55,520
If the system ranks passages, a relevant

48
00:01:55,540 --> 00:01:58,870
claim split across two passages may leave

49
00:01:58,890 --> 00:02:01,112
neither unit with enough evidence.

50
00:02:01,300 --> 00:02:03,123
The whole document can contain the answer

51
00:02:03,143 --> 00:02:05,494
while each searchable unit carries only

52
00:02:05,514 --> 00:02:06,331
part of it.

53
00:02:06,903 --> 00:02:09,018
And a typed word missing from the visible

54
00:02:09,038 --> 00:02:11,531
excerpt is a different question from a

55
00:02:11,551 --> 00:02:12,600
missing record.

56
00:02:12,762 --> 00:02:15,345
A match may occur in another indexed field

57
00:02:15,365 --> 00:02:18,451
or version. Revisit analysis and matching

58
00:02:18,471 --> 00:02:20,770
explanations before deciding what the

59
00:02:20,790 --> 00:02:22,239
interface has proved.

60
00:02:23,128 --> 00:02:25,703
Once eligibility is established, the

61
00:02:25,723 --> 00:02:28,589
chapter offers four diagnostic lenses.

62
00:02:28,764 --> 00:02:31,399
Vocabulary mismatch compares a query’s

63
00:02:31,419 --> 00:02:33,357
language with a relevant record.

64
00:02:33,519 --> 00:02:36,502
Out of vocabulary is relative to a named

65
00:02:36,522 --> 00:02:39,569
vocabulary. Out of distribution compares

66
00:02:39,589 --> 00:02:41,076
training with deployment.

67
00:02:41,238 --> 00:02:43,190
Composition asks whether matching

68
00:02:43,210 --> 00:02:45,715
preserved the required relationship.

69
00:02:46,275 --> 00:02:48,613
These are prompts for investigation, not

70
00:02:48,633 --> 00:02:51,860
exhaustive or mutually exclusive boxes.

71
00:02:52,010 --> 00:02:54,670
A specialised identifier can be poorly

72
00:02:54,690 --> 00:02:58,213
represented inside an unfamiliar corpus.

73
00:02:58,388 --> 00:03:01,267
One paper can support several hypotheses,

74
00:03:01,391 --> 00:03:03,188
which require different evidence and

75
00:03:03,208 --> 00:03:04,425
different remedies.

76
00:03:05,334 --> 00:03:07,278
The source example searches for heart

77
00:03:07,298 --> 00:03:10,035
attack recovery, while the relevant title

78
00:03:10,120 --> 00:03:12,381
is Rehabilitation after myocardial

79
00:03:12,401 --> 00:03:15,319
infarction. That visible relationship is

80
00:03:15,339 --> 00:03:17,135
vocabulary mismatch.

81
00:03:17,298 --> 00:03:19,804
Neither expression is necessarily absent

82
00:03:19,824 --> 00:03:22,535
from the index or model vocabulary.

83
00:03:22,710 --> 00:03:25,345
Different wording alone does not establish

84
00:03:25,365 --> 00:03:26,684
out of vocabulary.

85
00:03:27,267 --> 00:03:29,603
Librarians already build bridges with

86
00:03:29,623 --> 00:03:32,593
synonyms, controlled vocabulary, spelling

87
00:03:32,613 --> 00:03:35,763
variants, citation searching and iterative

88
00:03:35,783 --> 00:03:38,250
reformulation. Boolean OR can make an

89
00:03:38,270 --> 00:03:39,924
alternative term explicit.

90
00:03:40,087 --> 00:03:42,361
Query transformation can add a bridge

91
00:03:42,381 --> 00:03:44,925
automatically, but the generated input

92
00:03:44,945 --> 00:03:46,445
still needs checking.

93
00:03:47,359 --> 00:03:50,263
BM twenty five changes ranking, not term

94
00:03:50,283 --> 00:03:52,815
identity. It can use partial lexical

95
00:03:52,835 --> 00:03:55,276
overlap, and analysis may connect

96
00:03:55,296 --> 00:03:57,054
morphological variants.

97
00:03:57,203 --> 00:03:59,451
Its formula does not itself make heart

98
00:03:59,471 --> 00:04:01,707
attack synonymous with myocardial

99
00:04:01,727 --> 00:04:04,348
infarction. Do not credit the scoring rule

100
00:04:04,368 --> 00:04:06,667
for an expansion performed elsewhere.

101
00:04:07,221 --> 00:04:09,729
A suitably trained dense retriever may

102
00:04:09,749 --> 00:04:12,294
connect the complete query and document

103
00:04:12,314 --> 00:04:14,110
without exact overlap.

104
00:04:14,285 --> 00:04:16,160
That is a newer response to an old

105
00:04:16,180 --> 00:04:18,892
problem, not a guarantee for every

106
00:04:18,912 --> 00:04:21,881
paraphrase. Compare the suspected bridge

107
00:04:21,901 --> 00:04:24,613
against known relevant records; hybrid

108
00:04:24,633 --> 00:04:27,499
retrieval is another remedy to test.

109
00:04:28,413 --> 00:04:30,720
Preserve the original query, known

110
00:04:30,740 --> 00:04:33,489
relevant record, visible limits,

111
00:04:33,652 --> 00:04:36,222
indexed-unit information and any available

112
00:04:36,242 --> 00:04:38,606
trace. Separate what you observed from

113
00:04:38,626 --> 00:04:39,649
what you inferred.

114
00:04:39,812 --> 00:04:41,596
Then choose an intervention that could

115
00:04:41,616 --> 00:04:44,392
test the suspected loss of evidence.

116
00:04:44,967 --> 00:04:47,936
For a vocabulary mismatch, try an explicit

117
00:04:47,956 --> 00:04:50,501
synonym or controlled term and check the

118
00:04:50,521 --> 00:04:52,936
outcome. For an unknown candidate

119
00:04:52,956 --> 00:04:55,810
boundary, seek documentation or a trace

120
00:04:55,830 --> 00:04:59,469
first. Diagnosis accumulates evidence.

121
00:04:59,657 --> 00:05:01,519
The next film asks why encoding a word

122
00:05:01,539 --> 00:05:03,941
still does not establish that search can

123
00:05:03,961 --> 00:05:04,637
